<surname>Martucci</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Guo</surname><given-names>XJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Ramonetti</surname><given-names>JT</given-names></name><name><surname>Abreu Goris</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Newmark</surname><given-names>HL</given-names></name><name><surname>Lipkin</surname><given-names>ML</given-names></name><name><surname>De Cosse</surname><given-names>JJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Bertagnolli</surname><given-names>MM</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Cyclooxygenase-2 overexpression and tumor formation are blocked by sulindac in a murine model of familial adenomatous polyposis</article-title><source>Cancer Res</source><year>1996</year><volume>56</volume><fpage>2556</fpage><lpage>2560</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'Cancer Res||56|2556||bib3|'--><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8653697</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib4"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Dyson</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Buchkovich</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Whyte</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Harlow</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The cellular 107K protein that binds to adenovirus E1A also associates with the large T antigens of SV40 and JC virus</article-title><source>Cell</source><year>1989</year><volume>58</volume><fpage>249</fpage><lpage>255</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'Cell||58|249||bib4|'--><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">2546678</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib5"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Fisher</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Costantino</surname><given-names>JP</given-names></name><name><surname>Wickerham</surname><given-names>DL</given-names></name><name><surname>Redmond</surname><given-names>